# Coding Conventions

## Imports

Always use `@/` path alias. No relative imports between `src/` directories. Use `import type` for type-only imports.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
import { colors } from '@/theme';
import { View } from '@/components/ui';
import { useColorStore } from '@/stores/colorStore';
import type { AppStackParamList } from '@/navigation/types';

// ❌ BAD
import { View } from '../../components/ui';
```

## Exports

Named exports for all modules. `export default` only for top-level entry points (e.g. `App.tsx`). Each component domain directory has a barrel `index.ts`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
export function OnboardingScreen() { ... }
export const Text = forwardRef<RNText, TextProps>(function Text(props, ref) { ... });

// ❌ BAD
export default function OnboardingScreen() { ... }
```

## Components

- Use **function declarations** (not arrow functions) for top-level components
- Use `forwardRef` + `function` for base UI wrappers (`Text`, `View`, `Image`, `ScrollView`)
- Define styles with `StyleSheet.create()` at file bottom
- Component files: `PascalCase.tsx`

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
function MyComponent() {
  return <View style={styles.container}>...</View>;
}

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: { flex: 1 },
});
```

## Hooks

- Prefix with `use`, files named `use*.ts` (camelCase)
- Prefer `useCallback` / `useRef` for stable references
- Use `useMemo` for derived values

## Zustand Stores

- Store types use `type` (not `interface`)
- Use `getState()` for non-reactive reads
- Persist via MMKV `read/write` function pairs
- Expose snapshot getters alongside the hook:

```typescript
type ColorState = {
  currentHex: string;
  setColor: (hex: string) => void;
};

export const useColorStore = create<ColorState>((set) => ({ ... }));

export function getCurrentHex(): string {
  return useColorStore.getState().currentHex;
}
```

## Types

- Prefer `type` over `interface`
- Props: `ComponentNameProps`
- Navigation params: `*ParamList` unions
- Catch variables are `unknown` (`useUnknownInCatchVariables`)
- Array index access is `T | undefined` (`noUncheckedIndexedAccess`)

## Naming

| Category    | Pattern              | Example                     |
| ----------- | -------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Components  | `PascalCase.tsx`     | `OnboardingScreen.tsx`      |
| Hooks       | `use*.ts`            | `useCameraCaptureFlow.ts`   |
| Stores      | `*Store.ts`          | `colorStore.ts`             |
| Services    | `camelCase.ts`       | `authSession.ts`            |
| Types       | `camelCase.ts`       | `user.ts`                   |
| Constants   | `camelCase.ts`       | `api.ts`                    |
| Assets/Data | `*Assets.ts`, `*.ts` | `onboardingAssets.ts`       |

## Directory Organization

- **Domain-based** grouping under `components/`: `projects/`, `brands/`, `camera/`
- Each domain directory may include: components + `index.ts` + `*Assets.ts` + `constants.ts`
- `hooks/`, `utils/` are flat (no subdirectories)
- Tests mirror `src/` structure under `__tests__/`

## Internationalization

- Use `useTranslation()` hook via `t()` function
- Key format: dot-separated namespaces (`home.basics.cards.wooden.title`)
